&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Welcome to Planet. We believe in using space to help life on Earth.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet designs, builds, and operates the largest constellation of imaging satellites in history. This constellation delivers an unprecedented dataset of empirical information via a revolutionary cloud-based platform to authoritative figures in commercial, environmental, and humanitarian sectors. We are both a space company and data company all rolled into one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customers and users across the globe use Planet&#39;s data to develop new technologies, drive revenue, power research, and solve our world’s toughest obstacles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we control every component of hardware design, manufacturing, data processing, and software engineering, our office is a truly inspiring mix of experts from a variety of domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a people-centric approach toward culture and community and we strive to iterate in a way that puts our team members first and prepares our company for growth. Join Planet and be a part of our mission to change the way people see the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet is a global company with employees working remotely world wide and joining us from offices in San Francisco, Washington DC, Germany, Austria, Slovenia, and The Netherlands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Pre-Sales Senior Solutions Architect, you&#39;ll design complex solutions that demonstrate the value of Planet&#39;s data and services, helping organizations within the UK Defence and Intelligence community overcome critical Earth observation and geospatial challenges. You will act as a trusted advisor and value driver to prospective customers while working closely with product, engineering, and sales teams across Planet to champion customer needs. The ideal candidate, thrives in client-facing environments and has deep familiarity working within the UK Defence and Intelligence sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, remote position based in the UK. If located near an office, you are expected to work from that office 3 days per week. Up to 25% travel (domestic and international).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact You’ll Own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted advisor relationships with technical, operational, and executive leadership within customer accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical architecture and end-to-end design of solutions tailored to complex mission and operational requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver technical solution demonstrations and presentations, highlighting Planet’s capabilities and value to UK Government and Defence bodies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate technical workshops for operators and technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical responses for tenders, RFIs/RFPs, and unsolicited proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with internal Product, Engineering, and Customer Success teams to represent customer feedback and inform product roadmap priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attain quarterly and annual sales and operational objectives assigned by management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the needs of Planet&#39;s Defence and Intelligence customers to Sales leadership by communicating forecasts, pipeline opportunities, deal reviews, CRM data, and customer feedback.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior team members and lead internal knowledge-sharing sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience supporting the UK Defence and Intelligence community in a technical capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to obtain and maintain a UK Security Clearance (SC or DV).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep domain knowledge in Earth Observation, GIS, Remote Sensing, IMINT, and ISR mission workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working experience with ArcGIS, QGIS, SocetGXP, GDAL, Python, and other geospatial software packages and programming languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in geospatial system architectures, cloud environments/secure deployments, API integrations, and complex data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record translating customer mission challenges into scalable technical architectures and clear, high-impact demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional working proficiency in English, the language of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel up to 25%, including internationally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You Stand Out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active DV (Developed Vetting) clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct background as an imagery/geospatial intelligence analyst (IMINT/GEOINT) or operational user within UK MoD or allied intelligence services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in translating complex customer requirements into compelling, narrative-driven solutions, paired with a natural ability to command the room with senior defence executives, military leaders, and procurement authorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Deadline:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;11:45p / 23:45 CET on the date stated below. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis. This posting may be removed earlier than projected if a suitable pool of applications has been received. For this reason, we recommend applying as soon as you are able to.&lt;/p&gt;
